From 34b8566960cbc1788401da3e03cafaaef9c62dd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pavelgajdo <pavel.gajdo@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:12:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] vulkan, nup: bound the memory a scene load takes on
 Android

Ocarina of Time was killed for memory on a 12 GB phone entering its
first scene: graphics memory went from 0.65 to 3.7 GB in seconds.

- Transcode ASTC to BC1/BC3 a few layers at a time (64 MiB of RGBA8):
  each of its 90-layer 1365x1365 ASTC 8x8 arrays decoded whole into a
  ~900 MiB temporary image.
- Keep only decode images of 32 MiB or less for reuse (64 MiB in all,
  was 256): a 6144x6144 ASTC texture's ~200 MiB one stayed around.
- Free upload and device-local staging buffers of 16 MiB and up every
  frame once the GPU is done; one level a frame left ~500 MiB of the
  load's texture uploads pooled.
- Cap the NUP decompression cache at 128 MiB on Android (512 MiB
  elsewhere); larger members spill to a file.

Tested on a Galaxy S26 with the cap and trimming of the next commit: the
first scene loads with ~2.9 GB of graphics memory (was 3.3-3.7 GB).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b181701b3d3bb5720d31fb03f5ecc934c0c30a8d)
